   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Ser, tener, and llevar in descriptions",
     "texto": [
      "For general appearance, use **ser** + adjective: **es alto**, **es morena**, **es calvo**.\n\nFor facial features, hair, and eyes, use **tener** + definite article + adjective: **tiene el pelo corto**, **tiene los ojos azules**.\n\nFor accessories, facial hair, or clothing, use **llevar**: **lleva gafas**, **lleva barba**, **lleva bigote**.\n\nTo ask about someone’s appearance, say: *¿Cómo es?*"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Hair and eyes with tener",
     "texto": [
      "In Spanish, we use the definite article when describing physical features with tener:\n- *Ana tiene el pelo corto.*\n- *Él tiene los ojos verdes.*\n\nThe adjective agrees in gender and number with the noun it describes (pelo or ojos)."
     ],
